From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:24:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/29] board: mediatek-mobile: flush all DRAM before booting
 an OS

gd->ram_base/ram_size describe only the relocation window, and the by-VA
flush before an OS boot (CMO_BY_VA_ONLY) is clamped to it. bootm had moved
the kernel to 0xc0200000 and placed the initrd and FDT near 0x5e9ee000,
outside the window: after the MMU went off the kernel entry read stale
memory and faulted. Widen the range to the DRAM banks in
board_cleanup_before_linux(); unmapped no-map holes are skipped.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c         | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
index 2f83d51f91d..498c8d73467 100644
--- a/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
+++ b/board/mediatek/mediatek-mobile/mediatek-mobile.c
@@ -574,6 +574,26 @@ static void mtk_build_mem_map(void)
 	/* Zero size and attributes terminate the map. */
 }
 
+/*
+ * gd->ram_base/ram_size describe only U-Boot's relocation window, and the
+ * by-VA cache flush before booting an OS (CMO_BY_VA_ONLY) is clamped to
+ * it. Kernels, initrds and FDTs placed elsewhere would stay dirty in the
+ * cache when the MMU goes off. Widen the range to all DRAM banks; the
+ * no-map holes are not mapped, so the walk skips them.
+ */
+void board_cleanup_before_linux(void)
+{
+	u64 start, end;
+
+	if (!mtk_bank_count)
+		return;
+	start = mtk_banks[0].start;
+	end = mtk_banks[mtk_bank_count - 1].start +
+	      mtk_banks[mtk_bank_count - 1].size;
+	gd->ram_base = start;
+	gd->ram_size = end - start;
+}
+
 int dram_init(void)
 {
 	if (mtk_select_window()) {
